## 📐 8-Layer Architectural Failure Matrix

| Layer ID | Architectural Layer | Primary Failure Modes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **L1** | **Tool & Schema Contracts** | Casing mismatches, type coercion crashes, nested stringified JSON, missing keys, enum drift. |
| **L2** | **Retrieval & RAG** | Index staleness, semantic drift, empty context thresholding, chunk boundary truncation, poison doc retrieval. |
| **L3** | **Infrastructure & External APIs** | HTTP 429 rate-limit storms, expired bearer tokens, socket timeouts, upstream 503s, DB pool exhaustion. |
| **L4** | **Context Window & Token Limits** | Mid-generation JSON truncation, context overflow on recursive history, "lost in the middle" retrieval loss. |
| **L5** | **Orchestration & Routing** | Multi-agent ping-pong handoffs, intent misclassification, missing fallback gates, state loss across handoffs. |
| **L6** | **Retry Logic & Side Effects** | Double mutation on non-idempotent retry, unbacked-off retry storms, silent exception masking. |
| **L7** | **Model Behavior & Prompt Drift** | Cross-model delimiter breakage, over-eager safety refusals, system prompt injection via untrusted tools. |
| **L8** | **State, Cache & Concurrency** | Race conditions on shared scratchpads, dirty session hydration, stale cache hits overriding fresh DB state. |

