## 🛡️ How the Platform Mitigates Hallucinations

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Raw Trace Payload] --> B[1. Token Pruner Node]
    B --> C[2. Triage LLM Node]
    C --> D[3. Deterministic Grounding Verifier]
    D -->|Grounding Failed| E[Inject Critique Feedback: 'Evidence NOT found in trace']
    E --> C
    D -->|Verified 100%| F[Approved Output]
```

### 1. Deterministic Zero-Token Evidence Verifier (`src/verifier.py`)
All cited evidence strings in `cited_evidence` are verified via exact normalized substring matching against the raw trace text. Paraphrased or missing lines trigger a verification failure.

### 2. LangGraph Cyclic Self-Correction Reflection Loop (`src/pipeline.py`)
If citation verification fails, the pipeline routes back into the Triage Node with explicit feedback detailing missing lines, forcing the LLM to reflect and re-extract character-accurate substrings.

### 3. Pydantic v2 Schema Enforcement
Diagnostic output is constrained strictly to the `TriageDiagnosis` Pydantic model, forcing output compliance with the failure taxonomy.

